from the police in bristol detective  chief inspector from mainland somerset  police i'd like to give you an update on  the investigation into the missing  person  charlotte bevin and her daughter  yesterday lunchtime a member of the  public was walking along the cliff path  along the cliff face behind me  i noticed those distinctive white  slippers  that's very similar to the ones  charlotte was wearing when she left the  hospital the day before yesterday  and a multi-coloured blanket is quite  distinctive the member of the public saw  those on  the cliff side of a small fence and  thought they were suspicious  but didn't really know why  as a result of the media coverage  yesterday  that person put two and two together  effectively uh rang us at eight o'clock  yesterday evening and we attended the  scene and started with an extensive  search of the cliff face using uh  specialist  search teams and the force helicopter  unfortunately that led us to finding  the body of a woman  who has since been formally identified  as charlotte bevan  the search of the cliff face continued  throughout the night uh we're very keen  to try and locate  zany tiana who is charlotte's  newborn daughter  i regret to inform you that a short time  ago  on the cliff face  close to charlotte  the the body of a small baby girl has  been found  no formal identification has so far  taken place  but we anticipate that is going to be  charlotte's daughter  this is a a dreadful  awful frustrating business  and our thoughts are with the family at  this time  thank you very much
 

